    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Seldom do such opportunities present themselves to acquire a one-off lifestyle purchase in a beautiful scenic part of Co. Waterford.  Collins O’Meara Auctioneers are delighted to present Flower Hill to the market.  Situated on a South-facing elevated site overlooking the stunning Blackwater Valley, this delightful property ticks all the boxes.  Potential is endless for redevelopment as an agri-tourism business, equine enterprise, countryside accommodation etc. as the property boasts c. 28.8 acres of land and two residential houses.\r\n\r\nThe land is a mixture of quality permanent pasture and native woodland and habitat areas. c. 20 acres is laid out in a series of paddocks, currently used for grazing horses and sheep with characteristic mature trees dotted throughout the property with well-defined, established boundaries.  The orientation of the lands lends itself to endless walkways and leisurely country hacking by horseback.\r\n\r\nThe main dwelling house extends to 1,480 sq. ft. and is a split-level, three-storey detached residence in good habitable condition.  It is positioned on an elevated site with stunning countryside views, enclosed stone-walled garden, and a unique restored water-mill.  A second residence has been established in a beautiful stone courtyard, which is presented in excellent condition, boasting a host of old original features.  Together both residential units present a wide variety of accommodation options for prospective purchasers with the added advantage of a stone-built gate lodge, ripe for redevelopment.\r\n\r\nThis picturesque and historic property, whilst private and secluded, is within close proximity of Ballyduff, Lismore and Cappoquin so all amenities are just a short drive away."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Main House\t\r\n\r\nKitchen\t\r\n5.45m x 4.66m\t\r\nTile floor, floor and eye level units, tile splashback, Aga cooker, power points, access to rear.\r\n\r\nDining Room\t\r\n5.34m x 3.82m\t\r\nTimber floor, power points, radiator.\r\n\r\nW.C.\t\t\r\nW.H.B. and Toilet.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\t\r\n6.16m x 4.93m\t\r\nTimber floor, feature fireplace with stone surround, power points, radiator.\r\n\r\nSun Room\t\r\n5.03m x 3.85m\t\r\nTimber floor, power points, radiator, access to rear.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\t\r\n4.84m x 3.72m\t\r\nCarpet floor, built-in-wardrobe, power points, radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\t\r\n5.29m x 4.83m\t\r\nCarpet floor, built-in-wardrobe, power points, radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\t\r\n5.06m x 2.29m\t\r\nCarpet floor, power points, built-in-wardrobes, radiator.\r\n\r\nBathroom\t\r\n3.80m x 2.32m\t\r\nCarpet floor, shower unit, W.H.B., W.C., radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\t\r\n5.51m x 2.29m\t\r\nCarpet floor, power points, fitted wardrobe, radiator.\r\n\r\nCoach House\t\r\n\r\nLiving Room\t\r\n5.12m x 4.26m\t\r\nTimber floor, open fire with stove and back boiler, power points, T.V. point, radiator.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Area\t\r\n7.07m x 4.00m\t\r\nTile floor, floor and eye level units, power points, radiator, access to rear.\r\n\r\nBathroom\t\r\n3.75m x 2.26m\t\r\nTile floor, W.H.B. W.C., radiator.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\t\t\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\t\r\n4.05m x 3.75m\t\r\nCarpet floor, power points, radiator.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\t\r\n4.06m x 3.30m\t\r\nCarpet floor, power points, radiator.\r\n\r\nBathroom\t\r\n3.52m x 2.21m\t\r\nTiled floor, W.H.B., W.C., bath unit.\r\n\r\nServices:\r\n\r\n-Oil fired central heating in both properties.\r\n-Private septic tank serving both properties.\r\n-Private well water supply."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "-Idyllic country property with two residential units including stunning courtyard conversion.\r\n-Good quality grassland with four fenced paddocks, secure and watered, over-looking the Blackwater Valley.\r\n-Beautiful tree-lined driveway with gated entrance and detached gate lodge (in need of renovation).\r\n-Dual entrances to the property from two public roads.\r\n-Stone-cut buildings and outhouses dating back to 1818, situated within hand-cut stone archway.\r\n-Equestrian facilities including four stables and secure turn-out yard.\r\n-Array of mature gardens, natural forestry, habitat areas and stone-built enclosed walled garden.\r\n-Convenient location just five mins drive from Ballyduff Upper and 5 mins from Lismore.  Less than one hour to Cork Airport.\r\n-Endless potential as a guest house / Airbnb / equestrian facility or private residence.\r\n-8.64 Basic Payment Scheme entitlements with a value of c. €121.51 offered for sale with the land."
      },
